{
  "info": {
    "name": "Mountain Hut - E2E slots",
    "description": "End-to-end scenario for the slot and table management, run against the real running server.\n\nThe warden and tables 1 to 6 come from the seed, so start the server on a seeded db. For example, from the backend folder:\n\n    DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////tmp/mh_e2e.db SEED_DATA=true fastapi dev app/main.py\n\nThen run the collection in order with the Collection Runner or:\n\n    newman run MH_E2E_slots.postman_collection.json\n\nEvery run creates two new slots, Slot A (next Sunday, 12:00-13:30) and Slot B (the Sunday after, same hours), and 4 outdoor tables numbered after the highest existing one, so it can be repeated on the same db.\nChange `baseUrl` in the collection variables if the server is not on localhost:8000.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 - Warden defines Slot A, a Sunday lunch",
      "description": "Story: as a warden, I create Slot A for next Sunday at 12:00-13:30 and offer tables 1 to 6 in it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Warden logs in",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Session cookie is set\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.cookies.get(\"session\")).to.be.a(\"string\").that.is.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"luca.bonetti@rifugio.example\",\n  \"password\": \"warden\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Warden looks up the tables",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const tables = pm.response.json();",
                  "const byNumber = {};",
                  "tables.forEach((t) => { byNumber[t.number] = t.id; });",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Tables 1 to 6 exist (start the server on a seeded db)\", () => {",
                  "    [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].forEach((n) => pm.expect(byNumber, `table ${n}`).to.have.property(String(n)));",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// nothing below can work without the tables",
                  "if (![1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].every((n) => byNumber[n] !== undefined)) {",
                  "    postman.setNextRequest(null);",
                  "    return;",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"hallTableIds\", JSON.stringify([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].map((n) => byNumber[n])));",
                  "",
                  "// the outdoor tables get numbers no table has yet, so the collection can run again on the same db",
                  "const maxNumber = Math.max(...tables.map((t) => t.number));",
                  "[1, 2, 3, 4].forEach((i) => pm.collectionVariables.set(`outdoorNumber${i}`, maxNumber + i));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"outdoorIds\", \"[]\");"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tables",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "tables"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Warden creates Slot A (next Sunday 12:00-13:30)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// the next Sunday (a week from today if today is Sunday), and the Sunday after it",
                  "function ymd(d) {",
                  "    return [d.getFullYear(), String(d.getMonth() + 1).padStart(2, \"0\"), String(d.getDate()).padStart(2, \"0\")].join(\"-\");",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "// the hut is in Europe/Rome: +02:00 from the last Sunday of March to the last Sunday of October, else +01:00",
                  "function romeOffset(d) {",
                  "    const y = d.getFullYear();",
                  "    const lastSunday = (month) => { const last = new Date(y, month, 0); return last.getDate() - last.getDay(); };",
                  "    const md = (d.getMonth() + 1) * 100 + d.getDate();",
                  "    return md >= 300 + lastSunday(3) && md < 1000 + lastSunday(10) ? \"+02:00\" : \"+01:00\";",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "const sunday = new Date();",
                  "sunday.setDate(sunday.getDate() + ((7 - sunday.getDay()) % 7 || 7));",
                  "const nextSunday = new Date(sunday);",
                  "nextSunday.setDate(sunday.getDate() + 7);",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"sundayDate\", ymd(sunday));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"sundayStart\", `${ymd(sunday)}T12:00:00${romeOffset(sunday)}`);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"sundayEnd\", `${ymd(sunday)}T13:30:00${romeOffset(sunday)}`);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"nextSundayDate\", ymd(nextSunday));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"nextSundayStart\", `${ymd(nextSunday)}T12:00:00${romeOffset(nextSunday)}`);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"nextSundayEnd\", `${ymd(nextSunday)}T13:30:00${romeOffset(nextSunday)}`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 201 (slot created)\", () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const slot = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"sundaySlotId\", slot.id);",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"The slot starts on Sunday at 12:00 and ends at 13:30 (hut time)\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(new Date(slot.start_time).getTime()).to.eql(new Date(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"sundayStart\")).getTime());",
                  "    pm.expect(new Date(slot.end_time).getTime()).to.eql(new Date(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"sundayEnd\")).getTime());",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/slots",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "slots"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"start_time\": \"{{sundayStart}}\",\n  \"end_time\": \"{{sundayEnd}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
